  # a south-going hold slides about 6 units after it ends, a north-going one tens, so a dead-band pair cannot hit a 12 wide band
  # north standing (a slide there is harmless), then south crouched: a crouched player is a third as fast, so the slide after the hold is a few units, and the hull is already low at the hole
  @hold s-70 until sym=LOGIC_PLAYER_POS size=4 signed=true offset=8 op=ge value=-1060 timeout=60
